{
    desc => ':s/pat/repl/ substitutes first occurrence on current line',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/ex_substitute_line`

Tests the `:s/old/new/` ex command which replaces only the **first**
occurrence of a pattern on the current line.

**initial.png** — Buffer shows 2 lines with "hello" appearing twice on line 1.

Keys: `:s/hello/HI/<Enter>`

**after_substitute.png** — Only the first "hello" on line 1 changed to "HI".
Line 1 reads `HI world hello again`. Line 2 is untouched.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->ex('s/hello/HI/');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_substitute');
    },
}
__DATA__
hello world hello again
foo bar baz hello
